Hebrew Bible text — License and Attribution
===========================================

The Hebrew Bible text in this directory (texts/he/*.tess) is derived from:

  "Miqra according to the Masorah" (MAM) — a digital edition of the Tanakh
  based on the Aleppo Codex and closely related Tiberian manuscripts.
  Editor: Seth (Avi) Kadish ("Dovi").
  Source: https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/משתמש:Dovi/מקרא_על_פי_המסורה
  Obtained via Sefaria — https://www.sefaria.org/

License: Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0)
  https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/

Modifications by Tesserae V6: converted to .tess line-reference markup and
Masoretic paragraph markers ({פ}/{ס}) removed. The consonantal text is unchanged.

Under CC BY-SA 4.0 these Hebrew Bible text files are distributed under the same
CC BY-SA 4.0 license, with the attribution above. This notice applies to the
Hebrew Bible TEXT files (texts/he/*.tess) only; other components of Tesserae
(source code, models, and the ETCBC/BHSA-derived morphology tables) carry their
own separate licenses.
